### 0.24.8
- 2026-05-20: commit-pipeline supervisor now refreshes + re-links the workspace snapshot captured at queue time instead of the live `state.repos` — fixes pre-commit state reappearing (and the same work being re-committable) when the user switched workspaces mid-pipeline and navigated back.

### 0.24.7
- 2026-05-19: `discover_repos` no longer skips hidden directories — `.github` (GitHub's org/user-README repo) and any other dotfolder containing a `.git` is now picked up as a workspace row. The workspace's own `.git/` is still safely ignored (no nested `.git`).

### 0.24.6
- 2026-05-18: workspace switch via cache hit now kicks a background `kick_off_inline_refresh` after the instant swap so per-repo dirty/branch state catches up with any edits made while the user was on a different workspace (fs_watcher tears down watchers for away-workspace repos, so those edits were never observed and the cached state read as stale until Ctrl+R).

### 0.24.5
- 2026-05-18: `kick_off_workers` supervisor releases refresh locks by the Repo / ChildRef instances captured at queue time instead of looking them up in `state.repos` — fixes stuck `refreshing=True` rows that occurred when `state.repos` was replaced (workspace switch with cache miss, fresh discovery) between commit-pipeline acquire and the supervisor's finally.

### 0.24.4
- 2026-05-18: Ctrl+R inline refresh now surfaces a warn task `<repo>: refresh skipped — locked by another worker` for every repo whose refresh lock is held, so a stuck-refreshing row is visible in the sidebar instead of a silent no-op.

### 0.24.3
- 2026-05-18: README Windows install section now calls out `pipx ensurepath` + the "reopen terminal" step so `idlegit` resolves on PATH after install; documents the `%USERPROFILE%\.local\bin\idlegit.exe` fallback.

### 0.24.2
- 2026-05-18: `_read_version` falls back to `importlib.metadata.version("idlegit")` so the header shows the real version under pipx/wheel installs (the VERSION file isn't shipped to site-packages); `update.py`'s `main` now catches `KeyboardInterrupt` itself so Ctrl+C under the Windows console_scripts shim shows a clean "interrupted" line instead of a traceback.

### 0.24.1
- 2026-05-18: `idlegit-update` now works on Windows — registered as a console_scripts entry so `pipx install` generates an `idlegit-update.exe` shim, making the in-app "Check for updates → Update now" gesture functional on Windows.

